WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.301
-It is end of the week

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.803
and that's usually when I catch
up with some personal stuff.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.005
I check my inbox,
return some e-mails,

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.806
and of course,
send out thank you notes.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:07.807
And I was running a bit behind.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.008
And I wondered if I could
write out

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.743
my thank you notes right now.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:11.811
Hopefully --

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:16.316
[ Enthusiastic
cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.786
Uhh...oh.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.253
I should have...

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:22.288
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.389
Thank you. I should have --

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:26.425
[ Drum beating ]

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.495
I should have done this earlier
in the monologue.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.662
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.698
James, can I get something?
I don't know.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:35.868
Just noodle on the ivories.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:39.171
[ Laughter ]
[ Keyboard playing ]

00:00:39.171 --> 00:00:41.541
-That was your third record,
right?

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.075
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:46.312
"Noodlin' On the Ivories,"
with the apostrophe.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.681
Alright, here we go.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.382
Going to write out
some thank you notes.

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:53.619
[ Smacks lips ]

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:54.921
♪♪

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.290
Thank you,
the Trump boat parade,

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.926
for being the first parade
that replaced all the floats

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.628
with sinks.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.364
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.537
Thank you, Trump tell-all books,

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:14.807
for being the "Fast and Furious"
movies of the publishing world.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:18.010
[ Scattered laughter ]

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.748
[ Movie announcer voice ]
From the makers...

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.184
♪♪

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:27.386
[ Normal voice ] Thank you,
Martha Stewart's new CBD line,

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:29.589
for really adding confusion
to the sentence,

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.624
"My mom loves to bake."

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.960
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:40.366
♪♪

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.668
Thank you, pullout couches.

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:44.436
You may be uncomfortable
couches,

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:46.505
but at least you're
also uncomfortable beds.

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:49.842
[ Scattered laughter ]

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:52.211
[ New Yorker accent ] There's
a bar in the back of that.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:55.315
There's a bar in the mattress.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.619
♪♪

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.420
[ Normal voice ]
Thank you, Dairy Queen,

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.923
for releasing Blizzard-scented
candles

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.425
and somehow not being
the first time

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.961
I've been tempted
to eat a candle.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.628
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:10.763
-Come on.
-Yes.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.031
-Those Yankee cand--
They smell so good.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.267
-Hey, man.
-That's what I'm talking about

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.968
right here.
-You have one?

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.304
-Mm-hmm.
-Nice.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.140
-That looks like the candle
Ebenezer Scrooge, like --

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.476
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:28.848
-No, this is what they sell
in Yankee Candle.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.016
-Okay.
-Stuff like that,

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.117
the candle place.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:34.720
A modern candle
with candle drippings.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.858
This is not a cake.
-It's real Dickensian, like...

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:42.195
-You need a harpsichord.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.163
-Oh, man.
-Wait, what?!

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:45.632
[ Harpsichord playing ]

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:49.402
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:52.739
-Not bad.

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.673
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:56.476
-Wow.
-That was harder than I thought.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.677
I thought it totally was --

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.613
-Wait, what just happened?

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:04.083
-I was told it was a cake.
I thought it was a cupcake.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:08.254 line:0%
It's like a chocolate bar.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.823 line:0%
-That was a cup.
-God.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.391 line:0%
That wasn't even a cupcake.
That was a cup.

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:14.860 line:0%
-That was a cup.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.830
-I just ate porcelain.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.599
You don't see -- You can go
into a Yankee candle,

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:22.135
you see these candles
all over --

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.504
Bath and Body -- everything.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.439
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.574
It's almost like a Halloween
decoration kind of.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:31.811
Which, by the way, I just got
those pumpkins that move.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.246
Did you see those things?
-No.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.547
-It's a pumpkin.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.082
Man, they know how to do it
on Instagram.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:39.319
They give these ads, all of
my ads are for these pumpkins.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.355
How do they know I want these?
I bought it.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.624
-And you got one.
-It worked. Absolutely.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:47.259
The pumpkins,
they have a projector

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:49.795
in the plastic pumpkin and they
make the mouths move

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:51.930
and they talk and they sing
and stuff.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.733
And I totally got suckered
into doing it.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.535
-Yeah.
-You have them up already?

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:58.504
-I ordered them just in case.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.272
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, they're up already.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:03.375
-Sold out.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:05.911
It's Halloween year-round
in my house.

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.247
[ Chuckles ] Here we go.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.715
♪♪

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.051
Thank you, men named Todd,

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:15.288 line:0%
for making me imagine
a baby named Todd.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:20.259 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:23.429 line:0%
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.469 line:0%
I mean, it is solid --
-What flavor is that, yo?

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.337 line:0%
-I was told this was a cupcake.

00:04:32.337 --> 00:04:34.873 line:0%
This is --
Look at this thing, man.

00:04:34.873 --> 00:04:36.875 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
This is like actually eating

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:40.112 line:0%
a real candle. I should have
just ate a real candle.

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:42.448 line:0%
Is it a real candle?
-No.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:47.953 line:0%
-Got him.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:50.389 line:0%
-I just ate an actual candle.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:55.995 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
[ Scoffs ]

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:58.097 line:0%
I think it is.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.598 line:0%
-Oh, man.
-God.

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.134 line:0%
-Are you okay?
-No.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:03.202 line:0%
This is like I just ate wax.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.270 line:0%
-You're not going to be
the same.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.205
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:10.142
-Oh my gosh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:11.544
♪♪

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:12.611
Thank you, plates,

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.647
for being high-stakes Frisbees.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.948
There you have it, everybody.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.884
Those are my thank you notes.
-Don't eat a plate.

